* FD-06 / FD-15 / FD-16  FD inverting amplifier (gain -1, {{R_NET}} ohm) with a
* differential sine: each input moves {{AMP}} V peak in antiphase, so each
* output swings {{AMP}} V peak and Vod = 2*{{AMP}} V peak.
* FD-06: amplitude raised at {{FREQ}} Hz until THD(Vod) exceeds the limit (TRAN output swing).
* FD-15: THD at the bench amplitude and frequencies (spec 3.2.3.2).
* FD-16: frequency raised at the full-power amplitude until THD exceeds the limit.
{{SEED_OPTION}}
.lib "{{MODEL_LIB}}" {{CORNER}}
{{MC_PARAM}}
.include "{{DUT_FILE}}"
.temp {{TEMP}}
.options reltol=1e-6 abstol=1e-15 vntol=1e-9 method=gear
VDD vdd 0 {{VDD}}
VSS vss 0 0
IBIAS vdd ibias {{IBIAS}}
VCM vcm 0 {{VCM}}
VIP vip vcm SIN(0 {{AMP}} {{FREQ}} 0 0 0)
VIN vin vcm SIN(0 {{AMP}} {{FREQ}} 0 0 180)
R1 vip inp {{R_NET}}
R2 inp outn {{R_NET}}
R3 vin inn {{R_NET}}
R4 inn outp {{R_NET}}
XDUT vss ibias vdd vcmpin inp inn outp outn {{DUT}}
RVCM_DUT vcm vcmpin 1k
RLP outp vcm {{RL}}
CLP outp 0 {{CL}}
RLN outn vcm {{RL}}
CLN outn 0 {{CL}}
.control
set filetype=ascii
tran {{TSTEP}} {{TSTOP}} 0 {{TMAX}}
write {{RAW}} v(outp) v(outn)
.endc
.end
